From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmband: band track Clone, Join, PlayEx, GetParamEx/SetParamEx, seek, Download/Unload, Clear_All_Bands, IDirectMusicBand

The band track stubs returned S_OK without doing anything. They now:
- keep the bands sorted by their logical time (a band set in front of the others used to be put behind the first one);
- Clone ([start, end) moved to zero, the band in effect at start comes first at time zero, physical times moved too) and Join
  (this track before the join time, the other band track from it; E_POINTER, E_INVALIDARG for a negative time,
  DMUS_E_TYPE_UNSUPPORTED for another track class);
- Play: starting or seeking sends the band which is in effect at the start time; PlayEx converts the reference times; InitPlay keeps
  a play state for GetParamEx/SetParamEx (reference time in, music time through the performance); EndPlay releases it;
- SetParam: GUID_Clear_All_Bands, GUID_Download and GUID_Unload (the performance is the parameter), GUID_IDirectMusicBand;
  GetParam(BandParam) without a parameter is E_POINTER.
The todo_wine marks of the tests which pass are removed (the private band track interface of IDirectMusicBandTrackPrivate stays
todo: its methods are unknown). GUID_StandardMIDIFile is still not handled.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dmband/bandtrack.c b/dlls/dmband/bandtrack.c
index 45346ad..abfba78 100644
--- a/dlls/dmband/bandtrack.c
